@startuml
title the rolling back path, an aborted transaction and its redelivery
participant "Broker" as B
participant "TransferRequestListener" as L
participant "accounts database" as A
participant "xfers database" as X
participant "Transaction coordinator" as C
participant "__consumer_offsets" as O

B -> L : deliver the transfer request
L -> C : begin the Kafka transaction
L -> L : begin a JTA transaction over both databases
L -> A : debit the source and credit the destination
L -> X : write the transfer row and the PROCESSED_REQUESTS row
L -> L : a failure is thrown inside the JTA transaction
L -> A : Narayana rolls the accounts branch back
L -> X : Narayana rolls the xfers branch back
L -> C : abort the Kafka transaction
C -> C : PREPARE_ABORT, then the abort markers, then ABORTED
C -> O : the offsets are discarded
B -> L : deliver the same request a second time
L -> L : the second attempt completes and commits both branches
L -> C : commit the Kafka transaction
@enduml
